WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.950
Between collections,
alerts carry the news.

2
00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:07.145
Learn's page on deploying Service
Health alerts at scale names a built-in

3
00:00:07.145 --> 00:00:12.250
definition: configure subscriptions to enable
Service Health monitoring alert rules.

4
00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:16.945
It's assigned at a management group or
subscription, never a resource group,

5
00:00:16.945 --> 00:00:20.202
with a remediation task
so existing subscriptions

6
00:00:20.202 --> 00:00:22.625
get the alert rule too, not only new ones.

7
00:00:22.625 --> 00:00:26.512
With no parameters, the remediation
creates a resource group,

8
00:00:26.512 --> 00:00:30.018
the alert rule and an action
group in each subscription,

9
00:00:30.018 --> 00:00:33.600
and emails the subscription
owners for every event type.

10
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:38.104
The kit's alert policy script reads the
definition, checks its display name,

11
00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:40.938
and writes a plan with
two steps: the assignment,

12
00:00:40.938 --> 00:00:45.224
with a system-assigned managed identity
granted the definition's role,

13
00:00:45.224 --> 00:00:49.438
because only the portal grants it
automatically, and the remediation.

14
00:00:49.438 --> 00:00:53.139
It prints the plan's
SHA-256 and changes nothing

15
00:00:53.139 --> 00:00:56.651
unless it's run again
with apply and that hash.

16
00:00:56.651 --> 00:01:00.670
And never edit the alert rules
by hand: change the assignment's

17
00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:05.230
parameters and remediate again, or
the policy may overwrite the edit.
